// --- w17 (2026-08-25) - two flat-JPEG holders, both anchored on the accession the HOLDER issued,
// never on a title. gugg = www.guggenheim.org WordPress uploads. The rule is NOT [delete the
// trailing -1] (that is the upload-collision counter) but [strip every WP variant suffix back to
// the canonical stem <ACCESSION>_ph_web.jpg in the same uploads/<YYYY>/<MM>/ directory] - two of
// the 20 needed the stronger form and a literal -1 delete would have failed both. Ceiling is a
// ~4096px FIT BOX: -scaled, -2048x1386, _ph.jpg, _ph_print.jpg and ?w=8000 were all tested and
// are 404 or byte-identical. NO ACAO on any asset (measured on 30 with Origin: https://fuad.au),
// so these want the img.fuad.au /gugg/ alias - see .dtmp/tourqc-pass/w17/WORKER_GUGG.local.md,
// NOT pasted. Until it is, open-failed rebuilds on the direct url with cors:false, which is a
// plain image load and needs no CORS, so the degradation is benign and never worse than the plate.
// mnw = cyfrowe-cdn.mnw.art.pl: swap upload/cache/multimedia_big/ for upload/multimedia/. The big
// tier is a 1024px FIT BOX - measured, because the NAME IS A LABEL, NOT A SIZE (trap 9). ACAO * on
// all 48 with Origin: https://fuad.au, so no proxy and no worker change. 6000 px is an INGEST
// TARGET, not a cap and not [the original]: 15 masters land on exactly 6000, most fall below it,
// one exceeds it at 6620. Warning: 15 of the 48 are served content-type application/octet-stream
// with nosniff (the cache tiers are always image/jpeg) - the bytes are genuine JPEG, but eyeball
// garden-in-kissingen in a real browser once before trusting the set.
